add('vln_trans','INSPECTED CODE: The navigator constructs its translator representation from current candidate/panorama features and original language embeddings, then concatenates the speaker latent and soft-selected instruction representation (r2r_src_navigator/agent.py:310–390,700–746). Supervised sub-instruction and splitting targets enter losses after the representation calculation; this inspected path is not evidence of test-label leakage. The decoder consumes language embeddings directly, not generated text (model.py:207–310). Translator pretraining combines generation cross-entropy with three-negative triplet loss (r2r_src_translator/speaker.py:240–315). This confirms that a textual rewriting control must be separately implemented. The released training launcher specifies PREVALENT, Places365, AdamW, learning rate 1e-5, batch 16, maximum 15 actions and hard-coded author-local augmentation/checkpoint paths. The evaluator uses endpoint success within three metres and shortest-path SPL (eval.py:97–114). README provides processed R2R/R4R, SyFiS, features and checkpoint links, but its train_agent/test_agent launcher names differ from the available train_nav/test_nav names. No raw CLIP-based SyFiS construction script was found in the pinned tree. Processed data and checkpoints were not downloaded or executed; source inspection does not establish numerical reproduction.', ['VLN-trans/r2r_src_navigator/agent.py:310–390,700–746','VLN-trans/r2r_src_navigator/model.py:207–310','VLN-trans/r2r_src_translator/speaker.py:240–315','VLN-trans/run_translator/train_nav.bash:1–23','VLN-trans/r2r_src_navigator/eval.py:97–114','README.md'])
add('gela','INSPECTED CODE: GelDataset selects a trajectory/instruction/entity/box tuple and supplies span labels, landmark boxes and panorama-patch membership (ada_pretrain_src/data/r2r_tasks.py:600–650). forward_bbox explicitly computes span cross-entropy, sigmoid box regression with smooth L1 and generalized IoU, and bidirectional normalized token/patch contrastive loss (model/pretrain_cmt.py:351–424; gelunits.py:6–74). Adaptive pretraining averages task losses, backpropagates and applies scheduled/clipped optimizer updates (main_r2r.py:240–293). HAMT fine-tuning combines actor-critic and entropy terms with imitation loss; greedy inference selects the action-logit maximum (finetune_src/r2r/agent_cmt.py:349–388,487–523). run_r2r.sh specifies AdamW, 1e-5, batch 16, 300,000 iterations, PREVALENT augmentation and EnvEdit features. Thus training-data and augmentation controls matter when attributing improvements to grounding. README links Baidu-hosted annotations/features/checkpoints and GEL-R2R; these assets were not downloaded. The inspected code supports the stated objectives, not a claim of independently reproduced R2R/CVDN performance.', ['ada_pretrain_src/model/pretrain_cmt.py:351–424','ada_pretrain_src/model/gelunits.py:6–74','ada_pretrain_src/data/r2r_tasks.py:600–650','ada_pretrain_src/main_r2r.py:240–293','finetune_src/r2r/agent_cmt.py:349–388,487–523','finetune_src/scripts/run_r2r.sh','README.md'])
add('fgr2r','INSPECTED CODE: The official pinned release is a dataset and chunker release. source/make_subinstr.py invokes StanfordNLP, processes the three R2R instructions, and writes new_instructions; source/chunking_function.py implements dependency-root/conjunction/parataxis rules with special handling of short turning clauses. README distinguishes manually annotated chunk_view path indices (one-based), potentially singleton rotation/STOP chunks, and test instructions without sub-path labels. Its complete source tree contains the chunker and utilities, not the paper navigator, shift predictor, training objective or evaluator. Those components cannot be verified from this release; their dossier descriptions are paper evidence. No NLP model assets or annotated dataset were executed.', ['README.md','source/make_subinstr.py:1–41','source/chunking_function.py:1–89'], 'Official dataset/chunking source inspected; navigator training and inference implementation not included in the pinned release.')
add('gsavln','INSPECTED CODE: The released GR-DUET distinguishes training graph buffers from test graphs (agent.py:31–50). At test time batch size is asserted to be one; per-episode visited flags and stopping/step scores reset while graph topology and node embeddings persist (agent.py:581–654; graph_utils.py:95–132). agent_base.py:44–70 resets the persistent map once per evaluation environment, and main_nav.py constructs environments per scan. This confirms cross-episode scene memory rather than test-time gradient adaptation. Training reconstruction reads stored viewpoint panoramas and connectivity for previously buffered nodes, resets visited status, and computes graph representations (agent.py:342–377). Directly observed node embeddings overwrite accumulated candidate estimates; candidate updates stop after an overwrite. The code therefore supports a scene-sequence protocol, not independent fresh-map episodes. Only the GR-DUET path was source-inspected; the paper’s other backbones are paper evidence. Simulator data, pretrained models and scene-order sensitivity were not executed.', ['GR-DUET/map_nav_src/r2r/agent.py:31–66,342–377,581–680','GR-DUET/map_nav_src/models/graph_utils.py:95–139','GR-DUET/map_nav_src/r2r/agent_base.py:44–70','GR-DUET/map_nav_src/r2r/main_nav.py:64–84,225–248'])
add('same','INSPECTED CODE: CrossmodalEncoder forms routing input from text CLS and masked panorama embeddings and routes the query projection using selected experts (src/models/vilmodel.py:474–558,911–988). default.yaml and main_multi_q.yaml select Task routing, eight experts, top two, mixed R2R/REVERIE ScaleVLN plus PREVALENT/RxR/CVDN/SOON/ObjectNav data, and AdamW imitation/DAgger training. IMPORTANT RELEASE DISCREPANCY: TaskMoeRouting receives [batch, hidden] input, produces [batch, experts] logits, but applies softmax over dimension zero before selecting experts along the last dimension (lines979–984). DEDUCTION: batch composition can change an example’s routing; with batch size one every pre-top-k expert probability is one, so this path loses state-dependent expert selection. This is a source-level finding, not evidence that the reported paper experiments used this exact release or that their performance is invalid. src/trainers/base_trainer.py:208–280 performs task-weighted imitation/DAgger loss and optimizer updates. Main published evaluation cannot be reproduced confidently until routing-axis intent and checkpoint compatibility are resolved; no benchmark was run.', ['src/models/vilmodel.py:474–558,911–988','src/configs/default.yaml:1–140','src/configs/main_multi_q.yaml','src/trainers/base_trainer.py:208–280'])
add('walkreadless','INSPECTED CODE: The release is explicitly labelled an old, uncleaned version in README; final hyperparameters and VLN-CE code remain TODO. The inference rollout wraps language and panorama computation in no_grad and uses a persistent list of removed candidate viewpoints (map_nav_src/r2r/agent.py:476–571). BTP removes the earliest encountered unvisited nodes beyond its threshold from model input (agent.py:134–184). BGP normally preserves action-candidate features and ranks only background features; its action_included ablation can prune actions (models/pruning/bgp.py:107–206). VPP prioritizes tokens using a context-free irrelevant-token ID set, then restores the surviving tokens’ original order (models/pruning/vpp.py:1–99). These are tuning-free operations on an already trained navigator, not an untrained model. The main entry point runs evaluation and computes environment metrics. README’s admitted release mismatch and unreleased final hyperparameters limit paper-equivalent reproduction; no timing or FLOP experiment was executed.', ['README.md','map_nav_src/r2r/agent.py:134–205,476–571','map_nav_src/models/pruning/vpp.py:1–99','map_nav_src/models/pruning/bgp.py:107–206','map_nav_src/r2r/main_nav.py:190–240'])
put('mtrack',title='One Step at a Time: Long-Horizon Vision-and-Language Navigation with Milestones',implementation=n['mtrack']['implementation']+'\n\nINSPECTED CODE BY ASSIGNMENT 05: Official M-Track commit a7eaf93fc8631c9d1e7bbef437cc858b5b60f36a is materially incomplete. milestone_checker.py:7–30 implements substring matching and reachable flags, with no caller outside its own example. The inspected runtime does not establish paper-equivalent WordNet matching, interaction IoU, persistent checklist or proactive top-five rejection. agent.py:102–104 retains a target-tagger TODO; launcher files point at missing r2r_src/train.py. Assignment 05’s own AST-only test finds a syntax error in env.py line53 (evidence/05/mtrack_static_results.json); no fetched code was imported. CRF tagging, reachability BCE and CE rollout components are present. See evidence/05/code_audit.md for complete source ranges. This is an independently attributed static audit, not an executed navigation result.',repo_url='https://github.com/chanhee-luke/M-Track',repo_status='Official release independently inspected by assignment 05; incomplete runtime and syntax/launcher defects.',code_files=['Assignment 05: mtrack_src/milestone_checker.py:1–30; agent.py:96–115,236–345; env.py:53,106–165; train.py:1–90,250–268; eval.py:17–89','Assignment 05: milestone.py:18–95; milestone/src/model/transformer_crf.py:14–43; vision/alfred_head.py:31–123; vnn.py:156–203; run launchers'])
put('navnuances',implementation=n['navnuances']['implementation']+'\n\nINSPECTED CODE BY ASSIGNMENT 05 at pinned commit 57c0a58e89e198178a52f2bad067d8328c5aef9f: all six evaluator files, eval.py and math_utils.py were inspected. Direction-change Dual SR is joint left/right success, and direction checks use the first nonzero edge. Numeracy selects the positive reference closest to the endpoint and requires its coordinate nDTW to strictly exceed the best negative, with default one-metre scale. Landmark towards/past checks are geometric start/end tests, not full intermediate route verification. Region scoring uses final region and oracle-anywhere success. Base success is strict <3 m while numeracy allows ≤3 m. Submission loops lack a complete-annotation coverage assertion, so controlled experiments should check submitted ID completeness explicitly; there is no evidence published results omitted IDs. Full exact source ranges and reasoning: evidence/05/navnuances_code_audit.md. No project code was executed.',code_files=['Assignment 05: all six evaluators, eval.py and math_utils.py; see evidence/05/navnuances_code_audit.md'],repo_status='Official metric implementation independently inspected by assignment 05; no project execution.')
